## The toolchain's own compiler collects less often (mem.gc.5, ADR 1226).
## When the program being lowered is `compiler/main.ail`, its `main` starts
## with `rt.hg_wide()`, which lets the heap goal widen to five times the live
## bytes instead of three (`rt/native/heap_goal.ail`). A cold build allocates
## fast and keeps a modest live set: at three times it spent about half its
## time in the collector. Every other program is lowered as before and keeps
## the goal mem.gc.5 states; the source names no setting.

## Whether `file` is the toolchain's compiler entry, `compiler/main.ail`.
fn heapwide_entry(file str) bool
    hw_file := file.replace("\\", "/")
    hw_file == "compiler/main.ail" or hw_file.ends_with("/compiler/main.ail")

## The start of `main`: widen the compiler's heap goal before anything runs.
fn Lower.heapwide_enter(mut self)
    if fname == "main" and not is_rt and heapwide_entry(path)
        call("rt.hg_wide", [], Ty.Unit)
